From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 16:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: scp: use vfree for mailbox tables

scp_ipi_table_init() allocates the mailbox info, send and receive tables
with vzalloc().  The probe-error unregister path released those aliases with
kfree(), causing an arm64 translation fault when the fail-closed region-info
validation rejected a missing bootloader handoff.

Release all three tables with vfree() so a malformed or absent SCP handoff
returns the original probe error without crashing the calling modprobe task.

Signed-off-by: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/misc/mediatek/scp/rv/scp_helper.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/scp/rv/scp_helper.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/scp/rv/scp_helper.c
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/scp/rv/scp_helper.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/scp/rv/scp_helper.c
@@ -2974,15 +2974,15 @@ static void scp_device_shutdown(struct platform_device *dev)
 static void scp_device_remove(struct platform_device *dev)
 {
 	if (scp_mbox_info) {
-		kfree(scp_mbox_info);
+		vfree(scp_mbox_info);
 		scp_mbox_info = NULL;
 	}
 	if (scp_mbox_pin_recv) {
-		kfree(scp_mbox_pin_recv);
+		vfree(scp_mbox_pin_recv);
 		scp_mbox_pin_recv = NULL;
 	}
 	if (scp_mbox_pin_send) {
-		kfree(scp_mbox_pin_send);
+		vfree(scp_mbox_pin_send);
 		scp_mbox_pin_send = NULL;
 	}
 
-- 
2.51.0
